  "label": "Anti-Black Stereotype: Exoticization of Black Joy",
  "description": "The meme frames the children’s celebration as 'other' or exotic — a common trope in media that portrays Black joy as something foreign or 'authentic' in a way that is not aligned with mainstream Western norms. This exoticization can be used to justify or normalize the reduction of their experiences to simplistic or stereotypical imagery.",
